# Zymosis Tattoo — Project Rule

## Source of truth
- Read `docs/ZYMOSIS_PRODUCT_REQUIREMENTS.md` before major product/design work.
- Use `docs/ZYMOSIS_MASTER_BUILD_PROMPT.md` as the build brief.
- Update `docs/IMPLEMENTATION_STATUS.md` as substantial phases are completed.
- Never invent final artist biography, location, pricing, credentials, policies, or testimonials. Use explicit TODO placeholders.

## Product
- This is an artist portfolio + qualified tattoo inquiry funnel.
- Primary traffic is expected from Instagram/ManyChat.
- Preserve UTM/ref/ManyChat attribution into inquiry submission.
- Do not expand scope into scheduling, payments, portal or large admin unless requested.

## Art direction
- Target: 70% gallery/editorial, 20% sketchbook/pencil, 10% restrained graffiti.
- Artwork must dominate UI.
- Use negative space, extreme typography scale, editorial asymmetry, image-led composition.
- Avoid generic SaaS cards, pill-button overload, glassmorphism, gradients, neon, gold-luxury clichés, tattoo-shop skull/flame/grunge clichés.
- Pencil/graffiti details are accents only.
- Do not clone Oscar Akermo's exact layout, wording, code, typography treatment or assets.

## Typography
- Prototype with a legal/free neo-grotesk such as Inter Tight/Geist and Instrument Serif.
- Use `next/font` where appropriate.
- Never add unlicensed commercial font files.
- Large display headings: tight line-height, intentional wrapping.
- Micro labels: small but accessible and sufficiently contrasted.

## Stack
- Next.js App Router + TypeScript.
- Tailwind CSS 4.x plus custom CSS/design tokens as needed.
- GSAP/ScrollTrigger for complex timelines and scroll-linked motion.
- Lenis for restrained smooth scroll.
- Motion for React for component state/presence/gestures.
- React Hook Form + Zod for forms.
- Supabase for persistence/private upload storage when configured.
- Resend for transactional email when configured.
- Prefer Server Components by default.
- Scope Client Components narrowly.
- Do not add redundant libraries for capabilities already covered.

## Code quality
- TypeScript strictness: do not introduce `any` to avoid modeling data.
- Favor clear typed interfaces and discriminated unions.
- Keep business logic out of presentational components.
- Keep API/server input validation independent of client validation.
- Avoid premature abstraction.
- Delete dead code.
- Do not leave console debugging in production paths.
- Never commit secrets.
- Maintain `.env.example` when env requirements change.

## Motion
- Motion must reveal hierarchy, not decorate every object.
- Prefer transforms/opacity for smoothness.
- Centralize common easing/duration tokens.
- Clean up GSAP timelines and ScrollTriggers.
- Avoid multiple overlapping RAF loops.
- Parallax should usually stay within ±3–6%.
- Do not introduce scroll hijacking.
- Implement `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- Disable pointer-only effects on coarse/touch devices.
- Keep page transitions short enough that navigation feels responsive.

## Images
- Use supplied Zymosis assets or clearly labeled placeholders.
- Never reuse competitor artwork/images in production.
- Reserve aspect ratios to prevent CLS.
- Use responsive optimized images.
- Lazy load below the fold.
- Do not preload an entire gallery.

## Forms
- Use progressive multi-step booking UX.
- Preserve state between steps.
- Validate client and server.
- Use accessible labels/errors.
- Rate-limit public submission.
- Validate upload MIME/type/size server-side.
- Store body/reference images privately.
- Public clients must never be able to enumerate inquiries.
- Do not send sensitive form content to analytics.

## Accessibility
- Target WCAG 2.2 AA.
- All controls keyboard accessible.
- Visible focus.
- Menu/modal focus trap + Escape.
- No essential hover-only information.
- Respect reduced motion.
- Maintain usable contrast.
- Preserve browser zoom.

## Performance
- Hero LCP and mobile smoothness are priorities.
- Prefer Server Components and minimal client JS.
- Dynamically load noncritical interactive code when useful.
- Do not sacrifice Core Web Vitals for decorative motion.
- Avoid layout reads/writes inside hot scroll loops unless optimized.

## Workflow
Before major implementation:
1. inspect current repository;
2. read relevant docs;
3. state a concise plan;
4. implement the smallest coherent phase;
5. run format/lint/typecheck/build as available;
6. fix regressions introduced by the change;
7. update implementation status.

Do not perform massive unrelated refactors during a feature task.

## Completion checks
For meaningful frontend changes:
- test mobile + desktop composition;
- test keyboard;
- test reduced motion;
- check console;
- check overflow;
- run lint/typecheck/build.

For backend/form changes:
- test success;
- validation failure;
- upload failure;
- provider failure;
- duplicate/rate-limit behavior;
- verify secrets stay server-side.
